Both fall through to the receipt arm, so the two POSITIVE cases —
a_branch_named_for_a_ticket_no_commit_claims_is_named_and_red and
the_arm_refuses_on_a_trailer_gits_own_parser_cannot_see — fail: each asserts the
refusal NAMES the branch's ticket and the ticket the commits claim, which this
output does not.

The other six are FALSE-REFUSAL GUARDS. They cannot die from deleting the arm,
because they assert the arm does not fire; they die when it fires wrongly, which
is not hypothetical — section 4 above is two of them RED against the version of
the arm this branch already committed. Each also asserts the gate reached the
receipt arm, so a gate that died earlier for any other reason fails them too.

