### 9. bashrs, every finding mapped to the text that caused it
bashrs returns non-zero whenever it has anything to say, so its EXIT CODE
carries no information about this change. Both sides exit 1. The number
that carries information is ERRORS:
  base (origin/main:scripts/quorum-gate.sh): Summary: 0 error(s), 11 warning(s), 41 info(s)
  head (this branch):                        Summary: 0 error(s), 19 warning(s), 51 info(s)

The arm adds 8 warnings and 10 infos. Each one, with the exact text bashrs
flagged, read out of the file at the column it named:

  319  info    SC2089   col  5-61  flagged: 'trailers="$(git log --format=%B "$merge_base..$pushed")" '
  319  warning SC2086   col 51-58  flagged: '$pushed"'
  320  warning BRS0023  col  1-76  flagged: '        || die "could not read the commit messages of $merge_base..$pushed.'
  320  info    REL003   col 27-31  flagged: 'read '
  320  info    SC2162   col 27-35  flagged: 'read the '
  320  warning SC2086   col 55-66  flagged: '$merge_base.'
  320  warning SC2086   col 68-75  flagged: '$pushed.'
  334  info    SC2089   col  5-41  flagged: 'claimed="$(printf \'%s\\n\' "$trailers" '
  346  info    BRS0006  col 29-38  flagged: "'$branch' "
  346  info    SC2016   col 29-38  flagged: "'$branch' "
  346  warning SC2086   col 45-55  flagged: '$branch_id '
  347  warning SC2086   col 45-53  flagged: '$claimed'
  348  warning BRS0023  col  1-80  flagged: '     The branch name is read by gate A for the receipt path, by gate E for this'
  348  info    REL003   col 25-29  flagged: 'read '
  348  info    SC2162   col 25-32  flagged: 'read by '
  353  warning SC2086   col 19-29  flagged: '$branch_id '
  354  info    SC2230   col  1-66  flagged: '     misnamed -- which is the outcome the arm exists to prevent."'
  354  info    SC2023   col 18-26  flagged: 'which is '

Read them and they are one story. SC2086 fires six times on variables that
ARE double-quoted: bashrs loses quote context inside `$( ... )` (line 319) and
inside a multi-line `die` string (320, 346, 347, 353). BRS0023/SC2162/REL003
fire on the ENGLISH WORD "read" in two sentences of prose -- `could not read the
commit messages` and `The branch name is read by gate A`. SC2230/SC2023 fire on
the English word "which" in `which is the outcome the arm exists to prevent`.
SC2016/BRS0006 fire on `'$branch'`, quoted inside the message for a reader.

That leaves exactly two findings on real code: SC2089 at 319 and 334, both the
standard note that a single-quoted sed script or printf format is literal, which
is what those two lines intend.

The first version of this receipt said "all four are one artifact" while listing
SC2101 on a case PATTERN among them. Three lanes quoted that sentence back. The
case pattern is gone -- `[ -n "$claimed" ]` replaced `*[![:space:]]*` -- and the
claim above is narrower and checkable line by line.

